('2020-149','{{c1::Tetrabenazine}}, a VMAT2 inhibitor, is effective for Tourette tics refractory to antipsychotics and alpha-agonists.',''),
('2020-15','Puberty is initiated by a surge of {{c1::gonadotropin-releasing hormone}} (GnRH) from the hypothalamus.',''),
('2020-150','By age two, a child with normal language should produce {{c1::two-word combinations}}.',''),
('2020-151','A Schneiderian first-rank symptom of schizophrenia is {{c1::voices arguing}} or commenting on the patient.',''),
('2020-152','For postpartum depression in a breastfeeding mother, {{c1::sertraline}} has the lowest milk passage and strongest infant safety evidence.',''),
('2020-153','The {{c1::dentate gyrus}} is part of the hippocampal formation, whereas the amygdala and mammillary bodies are not.',''),
('2020-154','With normal aging, {{c1::verbal ability}} (crystallized intelligence) is the most preserved cognitive domain, while processing speed declines.',''),
('2020-155','Completed suicide risk in women peaks in midlife, around age {{c1::55}}.',''),
('2020-156','A spontaneous situation-specific thought like "I''m being left out again" exemplifies an {{c1::automatic thought}} in CBT.',''),
('2020-157','Pseudobulbar affect (uncontrollable laughing/crying) in multiple sclerosis responds to {{c1::amitriptyline}} (a tricyclic antidepressant).',''),
('2020-158','Combining linezolid (an MAOI) with an SSRI like sertraline causes {{c1::serotonin syndrome}}, marked by hyperreflexia, myoclonus, and clonus.',''),
('2020-159','Alzheimer disease pathology and atrophy appear earliest in the {{c1::hippocampus}} (entorhinal cortex).',''),
('2020-16','Narcolepsy (type 1) is confirmed by low or absent {{c1::CSF orexin (hypocretin)}} levels.',''),
('2020-160','Neck pain, progressive gait difficulty, and incontinence require immediate {{c1::MRI of the cervical spine}} to exclude spinal cord compression.',''),
('2020-161','Across evidence-based studies, a positive {{c1::therapeutic alliance}} most consistently predicts improved psychotherapy outcomes.',''),
('2020-162','On the WAIS, {{c1::vocabulary}} performance resists brain injury and is used to estimate premorbid cognitive functioning.',''),
('2020-163','The strongest risk factor for primary enuresis is a {{c1::family history of enuresis}}.',''),
('2020-164','Beyond falling testosterone, aging male sexual responsiveness declines partly from increased {{c1::sex hormone (testosterone) binding globulin}}, lowering free testosterone.',''),
('2020-165','Cigarette smoking induces {{c1::CYP1A2}}, increasing metabolism of {{c2::clozapine}} and lowering its levels.',''),
('2020-166','Under HIPAA, patients may be denied access to {{c1::psychotherapy notes}} kept separate from the general medical record.',''),
('2020-167','{{c1::Multisystemic therapy}} has the strongest evidence base for juvenile offenders and substance-using youth at risk of out-of-home placement.',''),
('2020-168','Word-finding difficulty with preserved knowledge of an object''s use is called {{c1::anomia}}.',''),
('2020-169','A primary advantage of genome-wide (hypothesis-free) mapping is that it can yield {{c1::novel, unexpected discoveries}}.',''),
('2020-17','{{c1::Cortical atrophy}} in the elderly stretches bridging veins, increasing susceptibility to chronic subdural hematomas.',''),
('2020-170','Escaping a public place to relieve panic symptoms strengthens avoidance through {{c1::negative reinforcement}} (removal of an aversive state).',''),
('2020-171','Compared with widows, widowers experience greater {{c1::mortality}} after bereavement.',''),
('2020-172','Early falls, axial rigidity, and impaired {{c2::vertical gaze}} on saccades suggest {{c1::progressive supranuclear palsy}}.',''),
('2020-173','Testamentary capacity refers to the ability to {{c1::make a will}}.',''),
('2020-174','When alleles at two loci co-occur more often than predicted by their frequencies, they are in {{c1::linkage disequilibrium}}.',''),
('2020-175','Periodic limb movements/REM behavior disorder presenting as kicking during sleep is confirmed by {{c1::polysomnography}}.',''),
('2020-176','A variable through which an intervention exerts its effect (anxiety reducing depression) is a {{c1::mediator}}.',''),
('2020-177','Private narrative speech during solitary pretend play in a preschooler is a {{c1::normal aspect of development}}, not psychosis.',''),
('2020-178','{{c1::Modafinil}} is FDA-approved to treat residual sleepiness in obstructive sleep apnea.',''),
('2020-179','Carbamazepine-induced {{c1::Stevens-Johnson syndrome}} is more common in Asians carrying the {{c2::HLA-B*1502}} allele.',''),
('2020-18','The {{c1::fishbone (Ishikawa) diagram}} is a quality-improvement tool that organizes possible causes of a problem into categories.',''),
('2020-180','Failure to meet the standard of care expected of a reasonable, prudent physician is termed {{c1::negligence}}.',''),
('2020-181','The appetite-stimulating hormone {{c2::ghrelin}} is secreted mainly by enteroendocrine cells of the {{c1::stomach and proximal small intestine}}.',''),
('2020-182','{{c1::Low serum iron}} is a risk factor for developing neuroleptic malignant syndrome during antipsychotic treatment.',''),
('2020-183','Spastic hemiparetic gait from a contralateral hemispheric stroke produces {{c1::circumduction}}, where the stiff extended leg swings outward in an arc to clear the floor.',''),
('2020-184','The hypothalamic {{c1::arcuate nucleus}} synthesizes {{c2::neuropeptide Y}}, a potent orexigenic peptide driving appetite.',''),
('2020-185','In Lewy body dementia, cholinesterase inhibitors most improve {{c1::behavioral disturbances}} (e.g., hallucinations, fluctuating cognition), not motor function.',''),
('2020-186','{{c1::Schizophrenia}} carries the greatest economic burden of chronic disability of any mental disorder, consuming healthcare costs disproportionate to its prevalence.',''),
('2020-187','Fluctuating cognition, visual hallucinations, parkinsonism, and REM sleep behavior disorder (dream enactment) form the core picture of {{c1::Lewy body dementia}}.',''),
('2020-188','Lithium''s antimanic effect has a delayed onset of about {{c1::1 to 3 weeks}}.',''),
('2020-189','Independent of prior depression, {{c1::caesarean delivery}} is a significant risk factor for postpartum depression.',''),
('2020-19','Interpreting that the patient consistently treats the therapist as an aggressor exemplifies {{c1::transference-focused psychotherapy}}.',''),
('2020-190','{{c1::Cognitive remediation}} has the strongest evidence for improving function during the recovery or chronic phase of schizophrenia.',''),
('2020-191','Depression arising during a period of escalating substance use is diagnosed as {{c1::substance-induced depressive disorder}} rather than major depression.',''),
('2020-192','During ECT, {{c1::lithium}} can prolong seizures and increase the risk of delirium, so it is often held before treatment.',''),
('2020-193','During normal adolescence, peer orientation increases, so {{c1::preferring to socialize with parents over peers}} is atypical.',''),
('2020-194','{{c1::Confrontation}} is the therapeutic intervention that draws the patient''s attention to a discrepancy, such as between affect and content.',''),
('2020-195','Among outpatients with schizophrenia, a history of {{c1::multiple psychiatric admissions}} is a significant risk factor for suicide.',''),
('2020-196','Intrusive, distressing thoughts that are recognized as unrealistic and neutralized by compulsions (e.g., praying) indicate {{c1::obsessive-compulsive disorder}}.',''),
('2020-197','The {{c1::hippocampus}} and parahippocampal gyrus mediate {{c2::declarative}} (explicit) memory for facts and events.',''),
('2020-198','With a hostile or coerced patient, the best initial response is {{c1::clarifying the purpose of the interview and defining a mutual agenda}}.',''),
('2020-199','With paranoid patients, prefacing symptom questions with {{c1::normalizing statements}} best builds rapport and reduces defensiveness.',''),
('2020-2','Erikson''s middle adulthood (40-60) task is {{c1::generativity}} versus stagnation, feeling useful by protecting future generations.',''),
('2020-20','Behavior maintained because each act produces a mood-lifting reward is explained by {{c1::operant conditioning}} (positive reinforcement).',''),
('2020-200','Social learning theory explains gender-typed behavior as based on {{c1::modeling}} of same-sex figures and reinforcement, e.g., maternal imitation.',''),
('2020-201','A {{c1::case-control study}} starts by selecting subjects already known to have (or lack) the outcome, then looks backward at exposures.',''),
('2020-202','Vygotsky''s {{c1::zone of proximal development}} is the range of tasks a child can master with guidance but not yet alone.',''),
('2020-203','Before puberty, {{c1::major depressive disorder}} occurs about equally in boys and girls; the female predominance emerges in adolescence.',''),
('2020-204','AMA social media guidelines recommend {{c1::documenting all electronic patient communication in the medical record}}.',''),
('2020-205','To detect common inherited variants of small effect contributing to disease, an {{c1::association analysis}} (rather than linkage) study is appropriate.',''),
('2020-206','The CATIE trial showed that second-generation antipsychotics were {{c1::no more effective}} than first-generation agents for schizophrenia.',''),
('2020-207','{{c1::Rett syndrome}} results from MECP2 mutations affecting a methyl-CpG-binding protein, making it the classic {{c2::epigenetically}} mediated disorder.',''),
('2020-208','{{c1::Rett syndrome}} is caused by mutations in {{c2::MECP2}}, whose protein epigenetically regulates gene expression via methyl-CpG binding.',''),
('2020-209','{{c1::Autism}} shows very high heritability, with monozygotic twin concordance rates of approximately {{c2::80-92%}}.',''),
('2020-21','The {{c1::orbitofrontal}} circuit mediates the capacity to inhibit hostile responses to aggravating situations.',''),
('2020-210','WHO global mental health strategy in low- and middle-income countries prioritizes {{c1::task-shifting}}: training non-specialist providers to identify and treat mental illness.',''),
('2020-211','Panic disorder requires recurrent unexpected panic attacks plus persistent {{c1::fear of further attacks}} or maladaptive behavior change.',''),
('2020-212','The quality of a clinical rating scale rests on reliability plus {{c1::validity}} (whether it measures what it intends to).',''),
('2020-213','In biofeedback, {{c1::electromyography (EMG)}} measures the {{c2::electrical potentials}} of muscle activity.',''),
('2020-214','Paternalism (overriding a patient''s wishes for their own good) is justified by the principle of {{c1::beneficence}}.',''),
('2020-215','In PTSD, functional imaging shows hyporesponsivity of the {{c1::ventromedial prefrontal cortex}}, impairing top-down inhibition of an overactive amygdala.',''),
('2020-216','Patients with autism spectrum disorder commonly show {{c1::impaired prosody}}, with monotone or abnormal speech rhythm and intonation.',''),
('2020-217','Sydenham chorea, with writhing limb movements after pharyngitis, is a poststreptococcal sequela of {{c1::group A Streptococcus}}.',''),
('2020-218','Implicit (procedural) memory consists of {{c1::mental models that summate multiple experiences}} and operates outside conscious awareness.',''),
('2020-219','When a delirious patient lacks decision-making capacity, the next step is to check for an {{c1::advance health care directive}} or surrogate.',''),
('2020-22','A key component of Collaborative Care integrating mental health into primary care is {{c1::care management}}.',''),
('2020-220','The most important physiological cause of low sexual desire in postmenopausal women is reduced {{c1::testosterone}}.',''),
('2020-221','Wake-promoting {{c1::orexin (hypocretin)}} neurons are located in the {{c2::lateral hypothalamus}}; their loss causes narcolepsy.',''),
('2020-222','Rising US incarceration from the 1980s to 2010s was driven largely by {{c1::mandatory minimum sentences for drug offenses}}.',''),
('2020-223','In late life, sleep architecture shows decreased {{c1::REM}} sleep, reduced slow-wave sleep, and more frequent arousals.',''),
('2020-224','First-line prophylaxis for cluster headache is {{c1::verapamil}}.',''),
('2020-225','Among psychiatric disorders, {{c1::depressive disorders}} account for the highest disability-adjusted life years (DALYs) in the Global Burden of Disease studies.',''),
('2020-226','Reliability of a rating instrument means {{c1::ratings are consistent among different raters}} (reproducibility), distinct from validity.',''),
('2020-227','First-line treatment for seasonal affective disorder is {{c1::bright light therapy}}.',''),
('2020-228','An anterior cerebral artery stroke affects the medial motor cortex, producing contralateral {{c1::leg weakness}}.',''),
('2020-229','The belief that the television sends messages meant specifically for oneself is a {{c1::delusion of reference}}.',''),
('2020-23','Delirium is suggested by a {{c1::fluctuating}} course, such as coherent speech on one exam and disorganized speech hours later.',''),
('2020-230','The {{c1::suprachiasmatic nucleus}} of the hypothalamus is the master pacemaker generating circadian sleep-wake rhythms.',''),
('2020-231','Unlike peptide hormones stored in vesicles, steroid hormones such as {{c1::DHEA}} diffuse out of the cell immediately after synthesis.',''),
('2020-232','The Chinese culture-bound syndrome {{c1::shenjing shuairuo}} (neurasthenia) most closely corresponds to the historical diagnosis of neurasthenia.',''),
('2020-233','To reduce liability in collaborative care, ensure {{c1::policies for handling behavioral health emergencies}} are in place.',''),
('2020-234','By {{c1::late school age (around 10 years)}}, the peer group first becomes an important mediator of aggression, especially in vulnerable boys.',''),
('2020-235','The most specific laboratory marker of heavy alcohol consumption is {{c1::carbohydrate-deficient transferrin}}.',''),
('2020-236','The collaborative care model centers on a {{c1::psychiatric consultant advising the primary care team}} about patients not improving, often via a care manager.',''),
('2020-237','Ziprasidone absorption is halved without food, so it must be taken with a meal of at least {{c1::500 calories}}.',''),
