('2020-241','Coarse facial features, broad hands, and a hoarse deep voice characterize Smith-Magenis syndrome, a {{c1::17p11.2}} deletion.',''),
('2020-242','CT imaging of the {{c1::posterior fossa}} is limited by beam-hardening artifact, whereas MRI visualizes it well.',''),
('2020-243','Addictions like gambling and opioid use disorder are driven by the mesolimbic dopamine pathway from the {{c1::ventral tegmental area}} to the {{c2::nucleus accumbens}}.',''),
('2020-244','A common side effect of vagal nerve stimulation during activation is {{c1::dyspnea}} (along with hoarseness and cough) from laryngeal/airway effects.',''),
