('2020-248','First-line treatment for catatonia (mutism, posturing, immobility) is a benzodiazepine such as {{c1::lorazepam}}, with ECT if refractory.',''),
('2020-249','Adult neurogenesis occurs in the olfactory bulb and the {{c1::hippocampus}} (specifically the dentate gyrus subgranular zone).',''),
('2020-25','Feelings of persecution most reflect the defense mechanism of {{c1::projection}}.',''),
('2020-250','Cerebellar Purkinje cells are inhibitory, releasing {{c1::GABA}} onto the deep cerebellar nuclei.',''),
('2020-251','The hormone {{c1::oxytocin}} enhances recognition of facial expressions and emotions and promotes social bonding.',''),
('2020-252','In the Strange Situation, secure attachment is shown when a child is {{c1::distressed at separation but readily comforted on reunion}}.',''),
('2020-253','In community-dwelling older adults, greater spirituality is associated with higher {{c1::resilience}}.',''),
