('2020-256','In healthy elderly adults, declining {{c1::attention}} most commonly impairs the ability to switch between tasks.',''),
('2020-257','The atypical antipsychotic {{c1::quetiapine}} (extended-release) is FDA-approved for adjunctive augmentation of antidepressants in major depressive disorder.',''),
('2020-258','The {{c1::NMDA}} receptor, by admitting calcium influx, is most critical for triggering long-term potentiation.',''),
('2020-259','Mirtazapine causes little nausea because it blocks the {{c1::5-HT3}} receptor.',''),
('2020-26','{{c1::Physical disability and reduced mobility}} contributes most to shrinking social networks in the elderly.',''),
('2020-260','Arguing that cognitive-enhancing stimulants should be available to all children to improve functioning rests on the ethical principle of {{c1::justice}}.',''),
('2020-261','The {{c1::habenula}} is an epithalamic structure that relays limbic input to midbrain monoaminergic nuclei and signals negative reward.',''),
('2020-262','A key epigenetic mechanism altering gene expression without changing DNA sequence is {{c1::DNA methylation}}.',''),
('2020-263','The parental task that first becomes especially important during toddlerhood is {{c1::limit setting}}.',''),
