('2020-265','The behavioral and visceral (autonomic) responses of fear are mediated by output from the {{c1::central nucleus of the amygdala}} to brainstem and hypothalamus.',''),
('2020-266','The group therapy factor of realizing one is not alone and others share similar problems is called {{c1::universality}}.',''),
('2020-267','The agency that accredits and inspects hospitals, sets care standards, and works on preventing medical errors is the {{c1::Joint Commission}}.',''),
('2020-268','In somatic symptom disorder, {{c1::lower educational level}} is associated with persistence of symptoms.',''),
('2020-269','The endocannabinoid with the highest affinity for the CB1 receptor is {{c1::anandamide}}.',''),
('2020-27','A smoker actively gathering cessation resources but not yet quitting is in the {{c1::preparation}} stage of change.',''),
('2020-270','Referring a schizophrenia patient to vocational rehabilitation is {{c1::tertiary prevention}}, reducing disability from established disease.',''),
('2020-271','DSM-5 somatic symptom disorder requires {{c1::excessive thoughts, feelings, or behaviors}} about symptoms, not that the symptoms be medically unexplained.',''),
('2020-272','Postpartum psychosis is most strongly associated with {{c1::bipolar disorder}}.',''),
('2020-273','In family therapy, expressed emotion refers to the level of {{c1::criticism, hostility, and emotional overinvolvement}}, which predicts relapse in schizophrenia.',''),
('2020-274','A {{c1::confidence interval}} gives a probability-based range used to generalize a sample estimate to the larger population.',''),
('2020-275','The precursor neurotransmitter from which melatonin is synthesized is {{c1::serotonin}}.',''),
