('2020-291','{{c1::Rapid return to alertness}} immediately after an episode favors psychogenic nonepileptic seizures over epileptic seizures.',''),
('2020-292','Therapy using direct measures to relieve symptoms and bolster self-esteem, ego functions, and adaptive skills is {{c1::supportive}} psychotherapy.',''),
('2020-293','Physical restraint is justified only when there is {{c1::imminent danger of harm to self or others}}, as with assaultive, escalating violence.',''),
('2020-294','During menopause, depression risk correlates most with the {{c1::rapidity of estrogen fluctuation}}, not its absolute level.',''),
('2020-295','Sudden isolated anterograde amnesia with repetitive questioning, resolving within 24 hours, is characteristic of {{c1::transient global amnesia}}.',''),
('2020-296','{{c1::Fragile X syndrome}} is caused by a {{c2::CGG trinucleotide repeat}} expansion in the FMR1 gene.',''),
('2020-297','In classical conditioning, a naturally fear-evoking stimulus like the explosion is the {{c1::unconditioned stimulus}}.',''),
('2020-298','STAR*D enhanced generalizability by incorporating {{c1::patient choice}} into its randomization (equipoise-stratified design).',''),
('2020-299','The characteristic EEG finding in delirium from metabolic encephalopathy is diffuse {{c1::slow-wave activity}}.',''),
('2020-3','The primary taste (gustatory) cortex is located in the {{c1::anterior insula}}, with the orbitofrontal cortex serving as secondary taste cortex.',''),
('2020-30','Rapid mood cycling, impulsivity, and instantly idealizing the new doctor while devaluing others suggests {{c1::borderline personality disorder}}.',''),
('2020-300','With aging, the {{c1::duration (and number) of nighttime awakenings}} increases, while slow-wave and REM sleep decrease.',''),
('2020-301','Diabetic neuropathic pain responds (independent of depression) to {{c1::duloxetine, venlafaxine, and gabapentin}}, not to NSAIDs or SSRIs.',''),
('2020-31','Bilateral visual aura with vertigo, dysarthria, perioral/limb paresthesias, and occipital headache characterizes {{c1::basilar migraine}}.',''),
('2020-32','Optic neuritis (painful vision loss, color desaturation, afferent pupillary defect) predicts later development of {{c1::multiple sclerosis}}.',''),
('2020-33','When a patient refuses recommended surgery, the most appropriate next step is to {{c1::assess decision-making capacity}}.',''),
('2020-34','Impaired rapid alternating movements indicates {{c1::dysdiadochokinesia}}, a sign of cerebellar dysfunction.',''),
('2020-35','NMDA receptor excitotoxicity kills neurons via {{c1::excessive calcium influx}} triggering mitochondrial caspase activation.',''),
('2020-36','Preoccupation with having cancer despite minimal symptoms, with checking and care-avoidance behaviors, indicates {{c1::illness anxiety disorder}}.',''),
('2020-37','Attributing one''s own anger to the therapist ("You must hate me") is the defense of {{c1::projection}}.',''),
('2020-38','An emotionally withdrawn child who fails to seek comfort despite responsive caregiving has {{c1::reactive attachment disorder}}.',''),
('2020-39','A boy with autism features, macrocephaly, hand-flapping, and family history of intellectual disability suggests {{c1::fragile X syndrome}}.',''),
('2020-4','{{c1::Construct validity}} assumes a theoretical model of the trait being measured and specifies how its components relate.',''),
('2020-40','REM sleep behavior disorder (dream enactment) frequently precedes development of {{c1::Parkinson disease}} and other synucleinopathies.',''),
('2020-41','Among medical specialties, {{c1::psychiatry}} carries the highest risk of physician suicide.',''),
('2020-42','Capgras delusion arises from a {{c1::prediction}} error: the familiar face fails to evoke the expected emotional response.',''),
('2020-43','{{c1::Major depressive disorder}} is the most common psychiatric comorbidity in patients with epilepsy.',''),
('2020-44','The {{c1::periaqueductal gray}} connects directly to the amygdala and is central to descending modulation of pain signals.',''),
('2020-45','A child qualifies for special education when a disability such as {{c1::intellectual disability}} causes inadequate academic progress.',''),
('2020-46','{{c1::Resilience}} is a personality characteristic that predicts successful aging.',''),
('2020-47','First-line pharmacotherapy for generalized anxiety disorder, especially with alcohol use, is an {{c1::SSRI/SNRI}} rather than a benzodiazepine.',''),
