('2021-256','Neural plasticity is mediated largely by rapid changes in number and morphology of {{c1::dendritic spines}}.',''),
('2021-257','Adolescents are best deterred from smoking by immediate cosmetic consequences like {{c1::bad breath and yellowing teeth}}, not distant disease risks.',''),
('2021-258','{{c1::Friedreich ataxia}} is a trinucleotide repeat disorder caused by a {{c2::GAA}} expansion in the frataxin gene.',''),
('2021-259','Balanced structural rearrangements like inversions and translocations are best detected by {{c1::fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH)}}.',''),
('2021-26','Group therapy for patients with psychotic disorders is best aimed at {{c1::social skills development}} rather than insight or personality change.',''),
('2021-260','The medication with the strongest evidence and FDA approval for binge-eating disorder is {{c1::lisdexamfetamine}}.',''),
('2021-261','Phenotypic differences between identical twins from environmental influence on gene expression are explained by {{c1::epigenetic}} changes.',''),
('2021-262','A functional (psychogenic) tremor characteristically shows {{c1::increased amplitude with loading}} and decreases with distraction, unlike organic tremor.',''),
('2021-263','Legally, every adult is {{c1::presumed competent}} until proven otherwise, regardless of psychiatric diagnosis.',''),
('2021-264','Justifying embezzlement by noting the company still profits exemplifies {{c1::rationalization}}.',''),
('2021-265','Oligodendrocytes form the {{c1::myelin sheaths}} around central nervous system axons.',''),
('2021-266','Withdrawal from {{c1::sedative-hypnotics}} (alcohol, benzodiazepines) can be life-threatening due to seizures and delirium tremens.',''),
('2021-267','A {{c1::missense}} mutation substitutes one amino acid for another, whereas a nonsense mutation creates a premature stop codon.',''),
('2021-268','Copy number variants are an important etiologic factor in syndromic {{c1::autism spectrum disorder}}.',''),
('2021-269','Naming the ink color while ignoring the printed word measures selective attention and inhibition on the {{c1::Stroop}} test.',''),
('2021-27','ECT became markedly safer in the 1950s with brief general anesthesia plus the muscle relaxant {{c1::succinylcholine}}, preventing fractures.',''),
('2021-270','The Civil Rights of Institutionalized Persons Act empowers the {{c1::US Department of Justice}} to intervene on behalf of institutionalized persons.',''),
('2021-271','The single greatest predictor of future violence is a {{c1::past history of violence}}.',''),
('2021-272','The orexigenic hormone ghrelin is secreted primarily by the {{c1::stomach}} (and small intestine).',''),
('2021-273','Resolution of separation-individuation, retaining an internal comforting parent image, marks {{c1::object constancy}}.',''),
('2021-274','{{c1::Naltrexone}} reduces alcohol craving by blocking opioid receptors and modulating dopamine in the {{c2::nucleus accumbens}} and ventral tegmental area.',''),
('2021-275','Dissociative amnesia risk is highest with trauma that is interpersonal and perpetrated by a {{c1::caretaker}}.',''),
('2021-276','Deliberate, recurrent fire-setting with tension beforehand and relief/gratification afterward, for its own sake, defines {{c1::pyromania}}.',''),
('2021-277','{{c1::Carbamazepine}} induces CYP3A4, lowering haloperidol levels through increased metabolism.',''),
('2021-278','Weight loss from refusing foods over sensory aversion, without body image concern, indicates {{c1::avoidant/restrictive food intake disorder (ARFID)}}.',''),
('2021-279','In conditioned taste aversion, the previously neutral apple flavor that now triggers nausea is the {{c1::conditioned stimulus}}.',''),
('2021-28','In current practice, polygenic risk scores are useful mainly to {{c1::predict prognosis}} in first-episode psychosis, not to diagnose individuals.',''),
('2021-280','Haloperidol metabolism is most affected by {{c1::carbamazepine}}; correction noted in 2021-277.',''),
('2021-281','Wakefulness requires inhibition of the sleep-promoting {{c1::ventrolateral preoptic nucleus (VLPO)}}.',''),
('2021-282','Subjects serve as their own pharmacologic controls in a {{c1::crossover}} study design.',''),
('2021-283','Per the WHO, the most common global barrier to mental health treatment is {{c1::low perceived need}}.',''),
('2021-284','Giving advice, praise, and encouragement to bolster coping and adherence characterizes {{c1::supportive psychotherapy}}.',''),
('2021-285','Valbenazine treats tardive dyskinesia by inhibiting the {{c1::vesicular monoamine transporter 2 (VMAT2)}}.',''),
('2021-286','{{c1::Hoover sign}}—pressing down with the paretic leg when raising the good leg—suggests a nonorganic (functional) leg weakness.',''),
('2021-287','Section 504 plans guarantee students with disabilities the {{c1::accommodations}} needed to access education.',''),
('2021-288','To maintain online professionalism, a physician should regularly {{c1::check their profile for accuracy}} and avoid sharing patient information.',''),
('2021-289','A warm parent who imposes few demands and lets the child avoid school exemplifies {{c1::permissive}} parenting.',''),
('2021-29','{{c1::Paroxetine}}, owing to its short half-life and anticholinergic effects, has the greatest SSRI discontinuation syndrome risk.',''),
('2021-290','Menarche and the possibility of pregnancy typically occur at Tanner stage {{c1::3 to 4}}.',''),
('2021-291','Copy-forward documentation is acceptable only when the data are {{c1::essential and pertinent}} to the current encounter.',''),
('2021-292','Early GWAS failed to identify psychiatric risk variants mainly because of inadequate {{c1::sample size}}.',''),
('2021-293','The dorsolateral prefrontal cortex is central to {{c1::working memory}} and executive function.',''),
('2021-294','In motivational interviewing, the best response uses an {{c1::open-ended question}} exploring the patient''s own view (e.g., the hardest part of quitting).',''),
('2021-295','Combined oral contraceptives induce glucuronidation of {{c1::lamotrigine}}, lowering its levels and often requiring a dose increase.',''),
('2021-296','Migraine typically {{c1::improves}} during the {{c2::second and third trimesters}} of pregnancy.',''),
('2021-297','Most drugs of abuse drive addiction by activating the {{c1::mesolimbic (mesoaccumbens)}} dopamine pathway from the VTA to the nucleus accumbens.',''),
('2021-298','In imprinting, {{c1::methylation}} silences one parental allele, so loss of the active allele yields unopposed expression and disease.',''),
('2021-299','Cognitive functions that decline with aging include {{c1::processing speed}}, response inhibition, and speed of {{c2::free recall}}, while vocabulary is preserved.',''),
('2021-3','{{c1::Oxytocin}} regulates osmoregulation, food intake, and female reproductive and sexual behaviors.',''),
('2021-30','A bilateral action/postural tremor that is absent at rest, improves with alcohol, and runs in families is {{c1::essential}} tremor.',''),
('2021-300','Psychometric testing surpasses clinical interview by enabling measurement of {{c1::validity}} and response patterns and eliminating ideological bias.',''),
('2021-301','Therapist factors most linked to a positive alliance are {{c1::genuineness}}, {{c2::empathy}}, and unconditional warmth (Rogerian conditions).',''),
('2021-31','Strong epidemiologic evidence shows regular cannabis use increases the risk of developing {{c1::persistent psychotic disorders}}.',''),
('2021-32','A parent mirroring a crying baby with a matched frown and soft voice illustrates a {{c1::contingent response}} fostering self-regulation.',''),
('2021-33','Natalizumab-associated progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy results from reactivation of the {{c1::JC (John Cunningham) virus}}.',''),
('2021-34','Inconsistent, distractible gait with buckling knees, waddling, and exaggerated retropulsion suggests a {{c1::psychogenic}} gait disorder.',''),
('2021-35','Federal regulations require nursing home residents be assessed with a standardized interdisciplinary instrument (MDS) at least {{c1::quarterly}}.',''),
('2021-36','The legal expectation of a psychiatrist evaluating suicidality is to perform and document a competent {{c1::suicide risk assessment}}, not to predict suicide.',''),
('2021-37','Inability to recall a stressful personal event with otherwise intact memory and normal workup indicates {{c1::dissociative amnesia}}.',''),
('2021-38','Promising quicker discharge in exchange for taking medication undermines the {{c1::voluntariness}} element of informed consent.',''),
('2021-39','DNA methylation of a gene''s promoter region silences transcription by {{c1::preventing transcription factors from binding}}.',''),
('2021-4','An autosomal dominant pedigree affecting every generation with anticipation is classic for {{c1::Huntington disease}}.',''),
('2021-40','Psychosis, dyskinesias, seizures, and autonomic instability with an ovarian teratoma indicate anti-{{c1::NMDA receptor}} encephalitis.',''),
('2021-41','Excessive intake of {{c1::pyridoxine (B6)}} causes a sensory peripheral neuropathy with tingling, pain, and numbness of the feet.',''),
('2021-42','The neuropeptide most implicated in panic disorder pathophysiology is {{c1::cholecystokinin}}.',''),
('2021-43','The ABPN maintenance of certification program requires ongoing demonstration of {{c1::medical knowledge}}.',''),
('2021-44','For ADHD in a patient with stable epilepsy on anticonvulsants, {{c1::methylphenidate}} is preferred and does not significantly lower seizure threshold.',''),
('2021-45','A child eating non-nutritive items (pica) should be screened with a {{c1::lead level}} given the risk of lead toxicity.',''),
('2021-46','The single best predictor of psychosis relapse within a year of a first episode is {{c1::medication non-adherence}}.',''),
('2021-47','Failure to perform smooth fist-rotation (one fist stays still) reflects loss of proprioception localizing to the {{c1::posterior column}}.',''),
('2021-48','Compared with men, women with schizophrenia typically have a {{c1::later age of onset}} and more prominent affective symptoms.',''),
('2021-49','Self-conscious emotions such as shame and humiliation typically emerge during the {{c1::preschool}} years.',''),
('2021-5','PTSD is most consistently associated with reduced {{c1::hippocampal}} volume on MRI.',''),
('2021-50','In postmenopausal women, low {{c1::testosterone}} is the greatest physiological contributor to sexual interest/arousal disorder.',''),
('2021-51','The HIPAA Privacy Rule requires physicians to give patients written {{c1::notice of privacy rights}} (Notice of Privacy Practices).',''),
('2021-52','Pervasive feelings of {{c1::worthlessness and helplessness}} suggest major depression rather than normal bereavement.',''),
('2021-53','{{c1::Last observation carried forward}} is the method used to handle participant dropout in clinical trial analyses.',''),
('2021-54','Dream enactment with kicking and swearing, plus parkinsonian signs, indicates {{c1::REM sleep behavior disorder}}.',''),
('2021-55','A clinician''s obligation to warn or safeguard identifiable victims of a patient''s threats is the {{c1::duty to protect}}.',''),
('2021-56','In epidemiology, the odds ratio is a measure of association that approximates {{c1::relative risk}}, especially for rare outcomes.',''),
('2021-57','The proportion of adverse events prevented by switching to a new drug is given by the {{c1::relative risk reduction}}.',''),
('2021-58','Bilateral vestibular schwannomas causing hearing impairment are characteristic of {{c1::neurofibromatosis type 2}}.',''),
('2021-59','The progesterone metabolite {{c1::allopregnanolone}} is a positive allosteric modulator of the {{c2::GABA-A}} receptor.',''),
('2021-6','For Alzheimer patients intolerant of oral cholinesterase inhibitors, {{c1::rivastigmine}} is available as a {{c2::transdermal patch}} to improve tolerability.',''),
('2021-60','Responding to a single target letter within a stream of letters (continuous performance task) specifically tests {{c1::attention}}.',''),
('2021-61','The {{c1::substituted judgment}} standard bases decisions on what the patient themselves would have preferred.',''),
('2021-62','A young child who self-blames for uncontrollable events like a parent''s death reflects {{c1::egocentrism}}, the inability to see beyond one''s own perspective in preoperational thought.',''),
('2021-63','{{c1::Fragile X syndrome}} is caused by a {{c2::monogenic (single-gene)}} CGG trinucleotide repeat expansion in FMR1, unlike contiguous-gene or chromosomal disorders.',''),
('2021-64','An infant who shows no distress on caregiver departure and little interest on reunion exhibits {{c1::avoidant}} attachment.',''),
('2021-65','For performance-only (situational) social anxiety, first-line pharmacotherapy is as-needed {{c1::propranolol}}, a beta-blocker that blunts autonomic symptoms.',''),
('2021-66','A wide-based, foot-slapping gait with a positive {{c2::Romberg}} sign reflects sensory ataxia, classically from {{c1::vitamin B12}} deficiency damaging dorsal columns.',''),
('2021-67','Major depression is associated with reduced {{c1::natural killer cell}} activity, evidence of immune suppression in depression.',''),
('2021-68','Among substance use disorders, {{c1::cocaine use disorder}} shows the highest heritability index of genetic contribution.',''),
('2021-69','{{c1::FDG-PET}} showing {{c2::frontotemporal}} hypometabolism best supports early frontotemporal dementia before structural atrophy is evident.',''),
('2021-7','The strongest evidence base for acupuncture supports its use in {{c1::pain management}}.',''),
('2021-70','For a depressed patient especially worried about sexual side effects like delayed ejaculation, {{c1::mirtazapine}} is preferred for its low rate of sexual dysfunction.',''),
('2021-71','The most significant risk factor for primary enuresis is a positive {{c1::family history}}.',''),
('2021-72','{{c1::Ghrelin}} is the orexigenic gut hormone that decreases latency to eat and increases meal size, opposing leptin''s satiety signal.',''),
('2021-73','Working memory relies on a distributed network with the {{c1::prefrontal cortex}} as its key cortical node.',''),
('2021-74','Frantic efforts to avoid real or imagined {{c1::abandonment}} is a core diagnostic feature of {{c2::borderline}} personality disorder.',''),
('2021-75','Activating the {{c2::GABA-A}} receptor opens a {{c1::chloride}} channel, hyperpolarizing the neuron and producing inhibition.',''),
('2021-76','{{c1::Sexual}} obsessions in OCD are more common in adults than in adolescents, who more often have aggressive/harm-related obsessions.',''),
('2021-77','In women 20+ years past menopause, hormone therapy with estrogen increases risk of {{c1::cardiovascular disease}}, reflecting the timing hypothesis.',''),
('2021-78','CSF that clears (fewer red cells across serial tubes) indicates a {{c1::traumatic lumbar puncture}}, whereas uniform bloody fluid with xanthochromia suggests subarachnoid hemorrhage.',''),
('2021-79','{{c1::Content}} validity is the degree to which an instrument''s items collectively cover the full domain of material it is meant to assess.',''),
('2021-8','{{c1::Beta}} waves are the EEG rhythm most associated with alertness and active concentration in the awake adult.',''),
('2021-80','Interpersonal therapy for grief helps the patient by better utilizing their {{c1::social support network}} to adapt to role changes after loss.',''),
('2021-81','In school-age children, a high level of {{c1::self-regulation}} is strongly correlated with competent social functioning.',''),
('2021-82','Constipation from clozapine results from {{c1::muscarinic}} (anticholinergic) receptor antagonism.',''),
('2021-83','Beyond atypical antipsychotics, {{c1::lithium}} is the most effective augmenting agent for depression with inadequate response to antidepressant monotherapy.',''),
('2021-84','Persistent pain adaptively downregulates the {{c1::dopamine}} system, reducing the motivation to effortfully pursue rewards.',''),
('2021-85','Using a patient''s mistrust toward the therapist (transference) to uncover defense mechanisms exemplifies {{c1::psychoanalytic}} psychotherapy.',''),
('2021-86','A unilateral resting tremor suggests Parkinson disease, best confirmed by a positive {{c1::L-dopa challenge}} showing symptom improvement.',''),
('2021-87','The Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale screens postpartum women effectively because it {{c1::de-emphasizes somatic symptoms}} that overlap with normal postpartum changes.',''),
('2021-88','Acute hallucinations with tachycardia, diaphoresis, and a clear sensorium in an irritable patient point to {{c1::alcohol}} withdrawal (alcoholic hallucinosis).',''),
('2021-89','{{c1::Lean}} methodology improves processes by eliminating non-value-added activities (waste).',''),
('2021-9','Pre-session self-report questionnaires chiefly benefit the psychiatric interview by {{c1::increasing the efficiency}} of the office visit.',''),
('2021-90','{{c1::Professionalism}} is one of the six ACGME core competencies taught and assessed in residency.',''),
('2021-91','Panic and avoidance triggered only by one situation (e.g., driving down steep roads), with no symptoms elsewhere, indicates a {{c1::specific phobia}}.',''),
('2021-92','Accepting a cookie from a guarded paranoid patient to build rapport is a benign {{c1::boundary crossing}}, not an exploitative boundary violation.',''),
('2021-93','On a coronal brain section, the {{c1::amygdala}} lies in the medial temporal lobe, anterior and superior to the hippocampus.',''),
('2021-94','Object relations therapy focuses on a patient''s {{c1::internalized representations}} of relationships with others.',''),
('2021-95','{{c1::Eugen Bleuler}} coined the term schizophrenia and distinguished primary (fundamental) from secondary symptoms (the four A''s).',''),
('2021-96','In puberty, the earliest hormonal change is {{c1::adrenarche}}, the increased adrenal production of {{c2::androgens}}, preceding gonadal maturation.',''),
('2021-97','A strong {{c1::therapeutic alliance}} predicts better outcomes in dialectical behavior therapy for borderline personality disorder.',''),
('2021-98','In collaborative care, the psychiatrist''s key role is providing {{c1::treatment recommendations}} to the primary care clinician for patients who are not improving.',''),
('2021-99','Maintaining a postured arm against gravity with resistance to repositioning is {{c1::catalepsy}}, a sign of catatonia.','')
insert into flashcards (question_id, cloze_text, extra) values
('2022-1','{{c1::Fibromyalgia}} is a chronic pain condition driven primarily by a central (non-nociceptive) mechanism known as {{c2::central sensitization}}.',''),
('2022-10','Excessive {{c1::NMDA}} receptor activation causes excitotoxic neuronal death in Alzheimer disease, the rationale for {{c2::memantine}}.',''),
('2022-100','An elevated CSF {{c1::white blood cell count}} (pleocytosis) suggests an underlying inflammatory or infectious process.',''),
('2022-101','A major limitation of the family-trio GWAS method is the difficulty of {{c1::collecting parental samples for late-onset diseases}}.',''),
('2022-102','Major depression and chronic stress share immune changes including {{c1::decreased B cells}} and reduced lymphocyte function.',''),
('2022-103','Neuroimmune studies of depression find {{c1::elevated pro-inflammatory cytokines}}.',''),
('2022-104','REM sleep first appears {{c1::in utero}} during fetal development.',''),
('2022-105','MAO inhibitors can cause deficiency of vitamin B6 ({{c1::pyridoxine}}), risking neuropathy.',''),
('2022-106','Changing the services covered by insurance is a {{c1::policy-level}} intervention.',''),
('2022-107','A school-aged child''s sense of personal worth is largely determined by their sense of {{c1::competence}} (Erikson: industry vs. inferiority).',''),
('2022-108','The risk factor most strongly associated with self-harm in prison is a {{c1::current psychiatric diagnosis}}.',''),
('2022-109','MDMA-assisted therapy shows preliminary efficacy for {{c1::posttraumatic stress disorder}}.',''),
('2022-11','In sexual addiction behavior mastery training, {{c1::risk management}} teaches patients to identify factors that raise the likelihood of symptomatic behavior.',''),
('2022-110','By about 18 months, a toddler can typically {{c1::copy/imitate a straight (vertical) line}}.',''),
('2022-111','A typical 3-year-old can {{c1::climb stairs unassisted}} (alternating feet).',''),
('2022-112','Benzodiazepine potentiation of GABA-A responses requires co-expression of the {{c1::gamma}} subunit.',''),
('2022-113','In an elementary-school child, difficulty with gross-motor tasks like {{c1::jumping and hopping}} is most concerning developmentally.',''),
('2022-114','Agitation from synthetic cathinone (bath salts) intoxication is best controlled with a benzodiazepine such as {{c1::lorazepam}}.',''),
('2022-115','An {{c1::interictal}} EEG (between seizures) typically shows slow, low-voltage activity rather than active ictal discharges.',''),
('2022-116','{{c1::Voyeuristic}} disorder requires the individual to be at least {{c2::18 years}} old for diagnosis.',''),
('2022-117','Dorothea Dix advocated for {{c1::better living conditions for the mentally ill housed in jails and poorhouses}}.',''),
('2022-118','A design in which each subject receives both treatments sequentially with a washout serves as their own control in a {{c1::crossover}} study.',''),
('2022-119','Postsynaptic GABA-B (metabotropic) receptor activation causes long-lasting hyperpolarization by opening {{c1::potassium}} channels.',''),
('2022-12','In a patient on a second-generation antipsychotic with low libido and menstrual irregularity, check serum {{c1::prolactin}} for antipsychotic-induced {{c2::hyperprolactinemia}}.',''),
('2022-120','Chronic traumatic encephalopathy from repeated head trauma shows accumulation of {{c1::tau protein}} on autopsy.',''),
('2022-121','Genome-wide association studies are especially powerful for detecting {{c1::common}} variants that each confer a {{c2::small}} effect on disease risk.',''),
('2022-122','{{c1::Electromyography (EMG)}} helps distinguish a functional disorder from a true motoneuron disease by detecting {{c2::denervation}}.',''),
('2022-123','A {{c1::paired t-test}} compares a continuous outcome measured in the {{c2::same subjects}} before and after an intervention.',''),
('2022-124','For a demanding, belligerent inpatient, the best approach is to {{c1::acknowledge the patient''s concerns and set firm limits}} rather than capitulate or switch teams.',''),
('2022-125','{{c1::Clozapine}} is the antipsychotic with the strongest demonstrated {{c2::anti-suicidal}} efficacy in schizophrenia.',''),
('2022-126','{{c1::Prader-Willi syndrome}} presents with infantile failure to thrive, then {{c2::hyperphagia}}, obesity, hypogonadism, short stature, and small hands and feet.',''),
('2022-127','A {{c1::case-control}} study assesses exposure-disease association using the {{c2::odds ratio}}, since incidence cannot be measured directly.',''),
('2022-128','Dementia with Lewy bodies shows {{c1::neuroleptic sensitivity}}, so {{c2::haloperidol}} can dangerously worsen rigidity and confusion.',''),
('2022-129','A lesion of the {{c1::optic chiasm}} produces a {{c2::bitemporal hemianopia}} by interrupting crossing nasal retinal fibers.',''),
('2022-13','Ascending weakness with areflexia after a vaccination or infection suggests Guillain-Barre syndrome, confirmed by {{c1::nerve conduction studies}}.',''),
('2022-130','Jurors weighing an insanity defense are most strongly influenced by {{c1::neuroimaging and biological evidence}}.',''),
('2022-131','Prescribing {{c1::multiple benzodiazepines}} to an elderly patient who then falls and fractures a hip is a likely basis for a {{c2::malpractice}} finding.',''),
('2022-132','Recurrent {{c1::compensatory behaviors}} (e.g., laxative abuse, purging) distinguish bulimia nervosa from {{c2::binge eating disorder}}.',''),
('2022-133','With normal aging after 65, {{c1::information processing speed}} declines while attention, language, and long-term memory are relatively preserved.',''),
('2022-134','The {{c1::cerebellum}} is among the first brain structures to complete {{c2::myelination}} in normal development.',''),
('2022-135','{{c1::Valproic acid}} should be avoided in women planning pregnancy due to high risk of {{c2::neural tube defects}}.',''),
('2022-136','A major consequence of {{c1::deinstitutionalization}} was the {{c2::transinstitutionalization}} of the mentally ill into prisons and jails.',''),
('2022-137','The APA position is that gun ownership should be restricted based on {{c1::increased risk of violence}}, not on a psychiatric diagnosis itself.',''),
('2022-138','Number needed to harm is {{c1::1 divided by the absolute risk increase}}; a 4% vs 2% mortality difference gives an NNH of {{c2::50}}.',''),
('2022-139','Seclusion and restraint of adult patients are associated with a significant increase in {{c1::post-traumatic stress disorder}}.',''),
('2022-14','An early step a public school takes for academic difficulty is initiating a {{c1::response to intervention}} (RTI) plan.',''),
('2022-140','Before a school-based psychiatric evaluation of a child, the first step is to obtain {{c1::parental consent}}.',''),
('2022-141','{{c1::Temperament}} refers to the heritable, automatic responses to danger, novelty, social approval, and reward, whereas {{c2::character}} is more environmentally shaped.',''),
('2022-142','Autism spectrum disorder is most consistently associated with {{c1::accelerated brain overgrowth}} during the first {{c2::four years}} of life.',''),
('2022-143','{{c1::Chromatin immunoprecipitation sequencing (ChIP-seq)}} identifies genomic DNA regions bound by a specific {{c2::protein}} of interest.',''),
('2022-144','The risk of schizophrenia in a person with an affected sibling but unaffected parents is about {{c1::10%}}.',''),
('2022-145','{{c1::Gq}}-coupled receptors activate phospholipase C, regulating the {{c2::phosphoinositide}} second-messenger system.',''),
('2022-146','{{c1::Disorganized-disoriented}} attachment is the infant attachment style most strongly correlated with a history of {{c2::maltreatment}}.',''),
('2022-147','Adoption studies show genetic risk for {{c1::completed suicide}} is elevated in offspring independent of the rearing environment.',''),
('2022-148','PTSD''s alterations in arousal and reactivity include {{c1::hypervigilance}}, {{c2::exaggerated startle}}, and sleep disturbance, irritability, or poor concentration.',''),
('2022-149','The corpus striatum comprises the {{c1::caudate, putamen, and globus pallidus}} (caudate plus putamen form the {{c2::neostriatum}}).',''),
('2022-15','The major site of Neuropeptide Y synthesis in the hypothalamus is the {{c1::arcuate nucleus}}, which drives appetite.',''),
('2022-150','Neuropeptides are derived from {{c1::mRNA translation}}, act via {{c2::second messengers}}, and have long half-lives, with release from both axons and dendrites.',''),
('2022-151','Beyond freedom from pain, terminally ill patients most often cite {{c1::preference for a specific dying process}} as important to a good death.',''),
('2022-152','The {{c1::suprachiasmatic nucleus}} of the hypothalamus is the master regulator of human {{c2::circadian rhythm}}.',''),
('2022-153','A declining number of {{c1::community mental health centers}} is associated with a higher rate of {{c2::suicide}} mortality.',''),
('2022-154','A broad public awareness campaign aimed at the whole population, regardless of risk, is {{c1::universal prevention}}.',''),
('2022-155','Melatonin is synthesized from {{c1::serotonin}} in the pineal gland.',''),
('2022-156','{{c1::Essential tremor}} is a postural/action tremor that characteristically improves with {{c2::alcohol}}.',''),
('2022-157','{{c1::Friedreich ataxia}} arises from a defect affecting frataxin and mitochondrial function, caused by a {{c2::GAA trinucleotide repeat}} expansion.',''),
('2022-158','Antagonism at {{c1::5-HT2C}} (along with H1) receptors drives the weight gain seen with some atypical antipsychotics.',''),
('2022-159','The strongest evidence for clinical decision making comes from a {{c1::meta-analysis}} of {{c2::randomized controlled trials}}.',''),
('2022-16','{{c1::Transactional}} group therapy encourages high intragroup dependence and reduced reliance on the group leader.',''),
('2022-160','{{c1::Klinefelter syndrome}} (XXY), suggested by tall stature, gynecomastia, and hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, is diagnosed by {{c2::karyotype analysis}}.',''),
('2022-161','A {{c1::safety plan}} is a prioritized, individualized list of supports and coping skills to use when a patient becomes suicidal.',''),
('2022-162','{{c1::Assertive community treatment}} most effectively reduces hospitalization and improves housing stability for the severely mentally ill.',''),
('2022-163','{{c1::Secondary amine TCAs}} such as {{c2::desipramine and nortriptyline}} are the least anticholinergic tricyclics.',''),
('2022-164','Measuring whether discharged patients receive timely follow-up reflects a {{c1::process}} quality measure under the National Quality Forum framework.',''),
('2022-165','The {{c1::amygdala}} is consistently activated by subliminally presented {{c2::emotional faces}} on fMRI.',''),
('2022-166','{{c1::Neutrality}} is the analyst''s equidistant stance among the patient''s id, ego, superego, and external reality.',''),
('2022-167','Higher {{c1::estrogen}} levels partly modulate the risk of {{c2::tardive dyskinesia}}.',''),
('2022-168','For refractory depression, high-frequency rTMS targets the {{c1::left dorsolateral prefrontal cortex}}.',''),
