('2024-183','Acute intermittent porphyria causes elevated urinary {{c1::porphobilinogen}}, producing the triad of {{c2::abdominal pain, neuropathy, and psychiatric symptoms}}.',''),
('2024-184','Compared to depression, anxiety disorders are more characterized by an {{c1::attentional bias}} toward {{c2::threatening}} stimuli.',''),
('2024-185','The most common side effect of head-mounted virtual reality systems is {{c1::motion sickness}} (cybersickness).',''),
('2024-186','The evidence-based treatment of choice for trichotillomania is {{c1::habit reversal therapy}}.',''),
('2024-187','By {{c2::12 months}}, a typically developing child first produces {{c1::single meaningful words}}.',''),
('2024-188','{{c1::Essential tremor}} is an action/postural tremor that worsens with arm extension and characteristically improves with {{c2::alcohol}}.',''),
